AUDIO: 'Still paying per envelope just to get a PDF [music] signed? OpenSign is the open source alternative to DocuSign, a full e-signature platform where you can sign documents yourself, request signatures from multiple people, enforce a signing'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'order, and get a tamper-evident completion certificate with a full audit trail at the end. It also comes with reusable templates, a built-in document vault called OpenSign Drive, an API,'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] and Zapier integration. We\'ll get into everything it can do in the [music] overview. OpenSign has a free cloud plan with unlimited e-signatures, with [music] paid professional and teams'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tiers that unlock API access, webhooks, bulk send, and team templates sharing. [music] Plus, an enterprise plan for custom domain, white labeling, and SSO. [music] Since OpenSign is open source, you can self-host it for free by'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
